 ### Offset Refinement Recursion
-A recursive inference step to refine noisy primitive positions by updating offsets $\Delta \mu_i$ based on previous estimation $\Delta \mu_{prev}$. Update rule: $\Delta \mu_i^k = \text{Tanh}(\mathcal{D}_{pos}(\mathbf{f}_i)) \cdot v_{size}$, where $\mathbf{f}_i = \mathcal{F}(\mu_i^{init} + \Delta \mu_i^{k-1})$. Stabilizes at a stationary point. On Waymo dataset, first inference increases PSNR by ~0.46 dB, subsequent updates maintain stable PSNR of 23.78 dB [S3].
