 ## Background
-Partially Learned Gradient Descent originates from the field of learned iterative reconstruction for medical imaging and tomography. It was developed to bridge the gap between model-based iterative reconstruction (which is interpretable but slow/hard to tune) and end-to-end deep learning (which is fast but lacks physical guarantees). The method unrolls the optimization steps of gradient descent into a neural network, allowing the network to learn the update rule (step size and momentum) while keeping the data fidelity term fixed [S1, unofficial]. It is implemented in the `learned_gradient_tomography` repository [S1, unofficial].
